A||N||4||Seanh||Redoing heads?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||11-07-2001||09:56 PM||||Alright, I have a pair of aluminum 2.8 heads I'm using for my engine. What I'm wondering is what parts to use to rebuild the heads. I want new valves, seals, retainers, and springs. Will the SS valves from the Fiero Store work in these heads? I should think they will right? Does anyone know of anywhere else that sells nice valves for this cheaper? OR and other head rebuilding itmes I'll need? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||11-08-2001||01:20 AM||||Hey Sean!<BR>How much tear down are you going to do?<BR>Some cam manufacturers make a kit to replace the cam, lifters and springs...<BR>And gasket kits usually come with valve seals...<BR>If your valves and retainers are not damaged, why replace them?<BR>Usually, you get a valve regrind and that takes care of 99.9% of any problems...<BR>If you are only going to swap heads, then get the heads overhauled...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||11-08-2001||01:23 AM||||I might have missed part of the story along the way, but...<P>You aren't going to just drop those aluminum heads onto your otherwise stock fiero are you?  If nothing else has changed, they'll live approximately one revolution.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||11-08-2001||01:44 AM||||Those aluminum heads won't bolt up to the Fieros intake or the accessories.<BR>If you change to another cars intake that does fit those heads then you'll have to use<BR>the donor cars DIS ignition and probably computer too so it's really not worth the hassle. Just work out the Fiero heads with a 3 angle valve job and some bowl porting and you'll have a little more performance.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||11-08-2001||09:03 PM||||Nope, I'v already got through the aspects of putting aluminum heads on the car, I just want to rebuild them... ||||reg||1
